summary:
Re-judgement after one fixer round.
(1) Every done_when item still holds, and all of the previous rework instructions were carried out:
- smooth road ribbons from map.roads, with other tiles layered on top (I checked the fixer's 1100x760 Chromium screenshot: diagonal streets are smooth, and the bridge deck and river edges are still tile-stepped, which is acceptable);
- traffic only on roads of 2 or more tiles;
- descriptive throws for missing document shops and BLO tent;
- the nits fixed.
(2) Locked tests are unchanged (forge tests verify). The new tests in test/world-roads.test.js add coverage for bridges over water, no building or wall under major roads, and the sparse-town shop fallback.
(3) No gaming: the throw broke locked T-2's sparse fixture, and the fixer answered with a real fallback (newShopPlot, deterministic, all-grass 3x3 plots with a reachable door at least 20 tiles from the office), not by weakening the test. It never fires on Pulivendula.
(4) Remaining minors are acceptable for now:
- newShopPlot repeats the house literal;
- nothing yet asserts that real towns avoid the fallback (carried into CP-2 as a learning);
- the T-5 HUD substring check is weak, but line 78 asserts the game's town.
(5) Decisions D-19, D-7 and D-18 hold.
(6) Ready to show: npm test 28/28, npm run e2e and design_check are green.
